# TivvleJoy core

- Visual work ends as PASS, FAIL, or BLOCKED. Never imply success from tests or code inspection alone.
- A rendered proof is required before any visual PASS.
- Do not invent proof paths, hashes, costs, or render results.
- Failed visual candidates are not promoted. Revert regressions.
- Use the strongest already-owned asset for each production role. Preserving a purchased archive does not require keeping a defective implementation visible.
- Approved camera, water, and character identity stay locked unless a later prompt explicitly authorizes a change.
- Prefer recoverable stacked draft PRs. Do not merge production PRs unless explicitly asked.
- Commit verified milestones, not noise after every tiny edit.
